The Software, including modified versions and works incorporating the
Software, may be distributed in source-code or closed-source form.
This License does not require distribution of corresponding source code.


2. Preservation of Origin

Any person who copies, modifies, incorporates, or distributes the Software,
in whole or in part, must preserve information identifying the origin of
the Software.

The following information is required (the "Required Origin Information"):

    Original Author: <original author>
    Original Project: <original project>

The Required Origin Information must not be removed, falsified, replaced,
or altered in a manner that misrepresents or obscures the origin of the
Software.

The following additional information may be provided:

    Original Repository: <repository URL>
    Modified: <modification status or description>
    Modified By: <person or entity>
    Contributors: <contributors>

Providing this additional information is optional.


3. InfoHeader

The Required Origin Information, together with any optional origin
information, is referred to in this License as an "InfoHeader".

When only a small number of source files from the Software are copied,
modified, or incorporated into another project, placing an InfoHeader
directly in each applicable source file is recommended.

When an InfoHeader is placed directly in an applicable source file, an
"Applies To" field is not needed. The file containing the InfoHeader is
itself the applicable scope.

Example:

    Original Author: Example Author
    Original Project: Example Project
    Original Repository: https://example.com/example/project


4. External Origin Notices

When many files, a directory, a substantial portion of a project, or an
entire project is copied, modified, or incorporated, the InfoHeader may
instead be placed in an external notice file distributed with the resulting
work.

Such a file may include, but is not limited to:

    THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES
    THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES
    NOTICE
    LICENSES

When an InfoHeader is provided in an external notice file, inclusion of an
"Applies To" field is strongly recommended.

The "Applies To" field should identify the files, directories, components,
or other portions of the resulting work to which the POL-licensed Software
corresponds.

Example:

    Original Author: Example Author
    Original Project: Example Project
    Original Repository: https://example.com/example/project

    Applies To:
        src/example/
        include/example/
        src/example.c


5. Binary and Closed-Source Distribution

The Software may be incorporated into and distributed as part of
closed-source software.

When the applicable source files and their InfoHeaders are not distributed
with the resulting work, the Required Origin Information must remain
available in material distributed with, included in, or directly accessible
through the resulting work.

This information may be provided through, for example:

    a README or NOTICE file;
    third-party license documentation;
    an About, Credits, or Legal Notices interface;
    documentation distributed with the resulting work; or
    human-readable information embedded in the distributed binary.

The method used is not required to disclose the corresponding source code.


6. Modification

Modification of the Software is permitted.

A person modifying the Software is not required to state that the Software
has been modified, identify the person who modified it, or provide a list
of contributors.

If such information is provided, it must not be used to falsify, replace,
or obscure the Required Origin Information.


7. Continued Preservation

Modification, translation, adaptation, refactoring, porting, combination
with other software, or incorporation into a larger work does not by itself
remove the obligation to preserve the Required Origin Information for
portions copied from the Software.

The extent of modification does not by itself remove the obligation to
preserve the origin of copied material.


8. Independent Implementations

This License does not impose its terms merely because a person has learned
from, studied, or understood the ideas, behavior, interfaces, algorithms,
or functionality of the Software.

Software independently implemented without copying the Software or portions
of the Software is not subject to this License solely because it provides
similar or equivalent functionality.


9. License Notice

A copy of this License, or a reference sufficient to identify this License
as the Preservation of Origin License, Version 1.0, must accompany
redistributions of the Software or portions of the Software that remain
subject to this License.

A short notice may satisfy this requirement if it identifies this License
and provides a practical way to find the full license text.

Where an applicable source file uses an SPDX license identifier, the
identifier for this License may be included in that file when such an
identifier is recognized by SPDX.

The use of an SPDX identifier does not replace the Required Origin
Information required by this License.


10. No Misrepresentation

Nothing in this License permits a person to claim authorship or original
project ownership of Software created by another person or project.

Additional copyright notices, authors, maintainers, contributors, project
names, and modification notices may be added, provided that the Required
Origin Information remains preserved and is not misleadingly altered.


